WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.390
- National Geographic and Mazda

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.410
started Assignment Inspiration,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.630
three quests to challenge photographers

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.230
to test their ability to tell
a compelling visual story

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.000
and to capture inspiring imagery.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.530
- Beth, Nina, Sam,

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.400
congratulations to each of you.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.480
Truly a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.170
to compete for a chance to photograph

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.860
for National Geographic Travel.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.590
- Just to be able to represent

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.640
both National Geographic and Mazda,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.070
I feel like I've been validated.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.440
So I'm bringin' my A game.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.310
- It's a big opportunity that lays ahead.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.780
I think I'm one step closer

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.390
to being a Nat Geo photographer.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:32.770
- It would be wonderful to win,

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.630
because what that means is that

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.640
someone saw the potential in me.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.710
- This quest is about capturing images

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.320
that define what it
means to uplift humanity.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.390
This, for me, really is about

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.560
the emotional connection that you make

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.080
between the people that you photograph

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.320
and the way that you
convey those emotions.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.550
- What's inspiring you
to click that shutter?

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.570
The challenge is to capture that emotion

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.040
and convey it through your photographs,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.780
so we can be inspired as well.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.390
- You will have only three hours

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:00.470
to photograph your subjects.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.380
It's gonna be tough.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.410
And in the end, you're gonna bring back

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.110
your five best images from each place.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.120
- And we're providing each of you

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.720
with a Mazda CX 30,

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.220
which we hope will
inspire you to inspire us,

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.930
to inspire everyone else who
sees your amazing photos.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.710
- When I meet a young photographer

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.000
who wants to do what I've
been lucky enough to do,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.100
I can't help but want to be a part of that

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.680
and help welcome them
into this amazing life

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.580
that I feel I have been lucky to live.

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:26.820
(upbeat music)

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.800
- At Mazda, we craft our
cars to inspire our drivers.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.450
Every interaction with the Mazda brand,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.740
we hope to uplift.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.630
It's what inspired Assignment Inspiration.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.750
- When I was thinking about
things that are uplifting,

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.210
I thought back to when
I started volunteering

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.750
at a local nursing home,
as a high school student.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.810
It left a lasting impression on me,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.440
changing the course of my life.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.883
That's how I decided to go into medicine.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:54.070
We're at a memory care home to capture

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.350
some nice moments with
Kids for Peace students

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.710
that are working on activities

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.120
with the residents here.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:01:59.953
Here we go.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:02.460
Kids for Peace,

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.960
they feel that through acts of kindness,

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.283
that can spread peace.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.160
That connection between a younger person,

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.460
who doesn't know that much about life yet

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.070
but filled with so much curiosity,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.500
and someone who has lived

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.510
with this wonderful perspective,

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:19.960
getting those fresh interactions,

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.060
that's when it's the most genuine.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.270
I need to be ready.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.360
The name of the game is flexibility,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.350
keeping my eyes open.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:28.920
Some of it's hard with angles.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.150
I want to be down more on their level,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.040
and I'll go to take a shot,

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.433
but then an arm comes in.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.350
That has been a challenge,

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.846
but it's fun to push yourself.

00:02:40.846 --> 00:02:43.096
(laughing)

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.080
- For me, being outdoors in nature,

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.902
it's like a reset button.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.160
(upbeat music)

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.510
It kind of puts me at peace.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.320
For Uplifted, I'm choosing to focus

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.120
on human and animal interaction

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.810
as it pertains to conservation.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:59.910
- Hey Sam, welcome!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:00.772
- [Sam] Hey, how are y'all?

00:03:00.772 --> 00:03:01.762
- Good to meet to you, finally.

00:03:01.762 --> 00:03:02.595
- Great to meet you.

00:03:02.595 --> 00:03:03.490
- Hi, I'm Denise.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.900
Welcome to Sky Falconry.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:05.733
- [Sam] Yeah, thank you so much.

00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:07.570
I chose Sky Falconry Ranch,

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:09.080
a place where people can come

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.050
and interact with birds of prey

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:15.010
in a respectful and natural sort of way.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.810
The emotional aspect of
the uplifted challenge

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.570
is incredibly captivating.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.340
- [Denise] If you can capture
how we feel every day,

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.980
then I think you're in the right place.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.280
- She could jump off at any second,

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.650
and there she goes (laughs).

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.070
- [Sam] But I'm worried about
what that's gonna look like,

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.220
especially having an entire crew around me

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.620
while I'm doing photography.

00:03:35.361 --> 00:03:36.700
(upbeat music)

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.240
- If I'm connected,

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.950
then people are going to see that.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.560
They're gonna feel that connection

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.410
and hopefully be inspired by my work.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.030
- A National Geographic
photographer needs to be curious,

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.380
curious about the world, compassionate.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.280
When you're intimately invested,

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.840
you tell stories that
are richer and deeper.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.690
It comes from the heart.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.140
- We are at Ride On Horse Therapy Center.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.610
What they do here is work
with special needs children

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.790
and teach them horseback riding,

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.500
motor skills, and how
to connect with animals.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.543
- [Trainer] You wanna pet her?

00:04:06.543 --> 00:04:07.980
There ya go.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.450
- I have two children
that have special needs,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.190
so for me to be able
to come out here today

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.250
and document this is a
really incredible experience.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.600
And I'm just in heaven.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.800
- [Woman] One, two, three.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.320
- Yeah, so what was
really beautiful is just

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.800
that these kids get to come out here

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.133
and just get to be kids for a moment.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.320
Time is flyin' by because
I'm havin' a great time,

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.640
and there's all this action,

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.910
and there's just never a dull moment.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.570
I'm trying to capture them goin' around,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.970
and it's a little bit challenging.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.730
It's interesting she's riding backwards.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.220
Not quite sure where I
should position myself.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.260
Just when I think I have it figured out

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:39.505
which way they're gonna go,

00:04:39.505 --> 00:04:43.247
the horses are like, oop, oop, oop.

00:04:43.247 --> 00:04:45.570
- The X factor in photography is often

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.990
about that moment that reveals how humans

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.283
have the power to uplift and be uplifted.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.440
- Children are inherently
inspirational to me.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.570
That energy that children bring

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:57.993
can be really healing.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.670
I mean, it just fills your heart.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:10.030
Being able to witness connections

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.953
that people are making, it's pretty sweet.

00:05:14.803 --> 00:05:15.636
- Whoa!

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:20.253
She is in massive hunting mode right now.

00:05:21.383 --> 00:05:22.750
- Oh.
- What was that (laughing)?

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:23.900
- She sneezed.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.430
- I didn't know birds could sneeze.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.220
Lots of action with these animals,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.460
so really trying to
capture their movements.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.380
They're really unpredictable.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.360
- If you don't have that
good working relationship,

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.860
it's hasta la vista, bud.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.050
- It's such a rare opportunity

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.230
to interact with birds of prey,

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.400
and it is such a gift

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.723
when they actually choose to come to you,

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.550
and especially when they
choose to come to our guests.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.150
We at Sky Falconry hold a special permit

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:56.090
that allows non-licensed
falconers the opportunity

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.950
of flying one of our birds of prey.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.480
- [Sam] I get that sort of adrenaline rush

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.020
that you get when you know that

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.563
something's happening and
it's a fleeting moment.

00:06:04.765 --> 00:06:07.040
- [Denise] Beautiful.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:09.980
- As this woman holds a
hawk for the first time,

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:11.423
her face lights up.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.890
This is the moment that I've been

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.730
looking for throughout the shoot.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.000
It's not something I
can ask her to recreate.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.200
That look on their face,
the sheer joy they got

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.643
is, for me, the definition of uplifting.

00:06:26.108 --> 00:06:28.436
(soothing music)

00:06:28.436 --> 00:06:30.275
- I'd love if my kids could
do something like this.

00:06:30.275 --> 00:06:31.547
How fun.

00:06:31.547 --> 00:06:34.550
All these volunteers
out here, it's amazing.

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:35.900
Really neat to watch
all the different things

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.190
that they do with the different kids.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:40.460
They really have it
tailored to their needs.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.170
So I wanna be far enough back so that

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.610
the children and horses'
reactions are natural,

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.350
but I do wanna make sure
that I'm able to capture

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:50.073
those uplifting moments
and not miss a thing.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.670
Such a great smile.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.530
- Oh my goodness, thank you.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.070
- They were givin' them so much smile

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:57.020
and love when they were walkin' around.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:04.610
- There were so many different
moments of connection.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.640
I don't know if I was snapping
the photos fast enough

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.053
to really convey that in the photos.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.740
But, I felt uplifted
the whole entire time.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.573
- How'd it go?

00:07:14.573 --> 00:07:15.540
- I think it went well.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.940
Yes, definitely gives me
all the feels (laughs).

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:25.410
- Really excited about the shots I got

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.730
and what I got to witness today.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.080
I put so much of myself into these photos,

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.240
but I don't ultimately have control

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.800
what someone's gonna take away from it,

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.250
and that's part of the vulnerability

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.480
of any art form.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.410
- I'm excited to go
home and see what I got.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.590
I know I'm gonna have
my work cut out for me.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.423
Picking five favorites is gonna be

00:07:42.423 --> 00:07:43.820
a really hard task.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.720
Just to watch these
children get an experience,

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.330
You know, to come out and do this thing

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.970
that they might not otherwise get to do,

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.690
to just be kids.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.170
I could just see how happy they were

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.960
and how much it meant to them.

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:00.403
It was really powerful and heartwarming.

